  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Slope from the angle",
    "body": "The segment from $C(8,0)$ to $B(13,y)$ makes a $30^\\circ$ angle with the $x$-axis, so its slope is $\\tan30^\\circ=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$. Then $\\frac{y-0}{13-8}=\\frac1{\\sqrt3}$, so $y=\\frac5{\\sqrt3}$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\frac{5}{\\sqrt3}$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "30-60-90 triangle",
    "body": "Drop a perpendicular from $B$ to the $x$-axis at $(13,0)$. The right triangle has horizontal leg $5$ and a $30^\\circ$ angle at $C$, so the vertical leg (opposite $30^\\circ$) is $\\frac{5}{\\sqrt3}$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\frac{5}{\\sqrt3}$**"
   }
  ],
