  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Three-digit integers are formed using only the digits 1 and/or 2. The sum of all such integers formed is",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "1332"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "333"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "999"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "666"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "1665"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Sum by place value",
    "body": "There are $2^3=8$ such numbers. In each place, half of them have a $1$ and half a $2$, so each place contributes $4\\cdot1+4\\cdot2=12$. The total is $12\\cdot100+12\\cdot10+12\\cdot1=1332$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1332**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Pair them up",
    "body": "Pair each number with its 'complement' (swap 1s and 2s): $111+222$, $112+221$, $121+212$, $211+122$. Each pair sums to $333$, and there are $4$ pairs: $1332$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1332**"
   }
  ],
