  "prompt": "Three straight lines, $l_1$, $l_2$ and $l_3$, have slopes $\\frac12$, $\\frac13$ and $\\frac14$, respectively. All three lines have the same $y$-intercept. If the sum of the $x$-intercepts of the three lines is 36, then the $y$-intercept is",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$\\frac{-13}{12}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$\\frac{-12}{13}$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$-4$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "4"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$-9$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Write the $x$-intercepts",
    "body": "With $y$-intercept $b$, the line $y=mx+b$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=-\\frac bm$. The intercepts are $-2b$, $-3b$, $-4b$, with sum $-9b=36$, so $b=-4$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $-4$**"
   }
  ],
