  "points": 6,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Square $ABCD$ has sides of length 14. A circle is drawn through $A$ and $D$ so that it is tangent to $BC$, as shown. What is the radius of the circle?",
  "image": "qimages/cemc/fermat-1998/q19.webp",
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "8.5"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "8.75"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "9"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "9.25"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "9.5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Coordinates",
    "body": "Let $D=(0,0)$, $A=(0,14)$, and $BC$ be the line $x=14$. The centre lies on $y=7$ (perpendicular bisector of $AD$) at distance $r$ from $x=14$: centre $(14-r,7)$. Then $(14-r)^2+7^2=r^2$, so $196-28r+49=0$ and $r=\\frac{245}{28}=8.75$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 8.75**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Right triangle with the chord",
    "body": "Let $M$ be the midpoint of $AD$ and $O$ the centre. Then $MD=7$ and $OM=14-r$, and $OD=r$: $(14-r)^2+49=r^2$ gives $r=8.75$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 8.75**"
   }
  ],
